From 0ef1fed2030756689caf8032318031a8c2c63301 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 20:01:57 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 8.5 branding sweep v2 (rendered UI strings)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 8 UAT surfaced "Chromium" still rendering in numerous user-facing
surfaces despite Phase 4.7's static-allowlist sign-off. Static analysis
proved insufficient.

This phase rewrites all body-text occurrences of "Chromium" to "phlink"
in the chromium-lane GRD/GRDP files, while preserving:

  - <!-- developer comments -->
  - desc="..." translator-help attributes
  - "The Chromium Authors" legal copyright attribution
  - "ChromiumOS" (we do not ship for ChromeOS)
  - <ex>Chromium</ex> translator examples
  - "same file as Chromium" / "Unused in Chromium" dev comments

Files modified:
  - chrome/app/chromium_strings.grd          (~130 strings)
  - chrome/app/settings_chromium_strings.grdp (~25 strings)
  - chrome/app/password_manager_ui_strings.grdp (7 strings)
  - chrome/app/settings_strings.grdp         (2 strings)

Validated by tests/branding-audit/runtime-audit.py (CDP-driven)
across chrome://settings/{,appearance,privacy,help}, chrome://version,
chrome://flags, chrome://about, and chrome://newtab — all PASS.

chrome:// URL scheme + chrome://about page contents intentionally
remain "Chrome URLs" — those are Phase 8.6's scope (BRND-09 scheme
alias).

Patch slot 0116/NN of Phase 8.5.
Refs phlink BRND-03, BRND-04.
